config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_ADA_P1_METER
	bool "Domoticz plugin: ADA P1 meter"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	default n
	help
		Support for the ADA P1 meter (greenhess.com), a reader that
		publishes the P1 telegram of a smart meter on the local network:
		the plugin polls it and creates the energy devices of the
		installation — imported and exported energy, the per-tariff
		counters, current power, and the gas/water values when the meter
		reports them.

		It is the counterpart of the
		FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_HOMEWIZARD_P1 plugin for owners of an ADA
		reader. Both can coexist: they create independent device sets.

		The plugin uses only the Domoticz module and the Python standard
		library, and its labels follow the language of the hardware entry
		(17 translations).

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> add the ADA P1 meter, enter the IP
		address of the reader and, where required, the Domoticz address
		(127.0.0.1) and its HTTP port (8080).

		Upstream publishes no license file, so the plugin keeps the
		licensing status upstream gave it; the build fetches a pinned
		commit of the main branch because there are no release tags.
